      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-09-21T11:19:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So between <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/kwmaxxh6i00l5r2/Quando%20Ahora.jpg?dl=0\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Quando? Ahora!</a>, <a href=\"https://sentinelswiki.com/images/f/f9/Bethegate.jpg\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Be the Gate</a>, <a href=\"https://sentinelswiki.com/images/f/f5/Timevtime.jpg\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Time v. Time</a>, and Ivana Ramonat and the Legacy of Destruction, we have a lot of alternate universe heroes and villains running around but not yet a whole lot of ideas of how they ended up so different from \"our\" versions or what their rivalries and battles were like.</p><p>So I was wondering if anyone had any pet theories or speculations that have been running around in their heads to share?</p><p>(Personally I still like my theory that in the Quando? Ahora! universe it was Nightmist who found the Bell and Anthony who was inspired to go find out <a href=\"http://www.arkhamhorrorwiki.com/Dexter_Drake\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">what happened to his grandfather that disappeared in the pursuit of real magic</a>. I always wondered if that matching of name was intentional on Christopher's part.)</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:50:10.696Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
